# Tools mobile product preview

Product Preview must show the colored garment and the shopper's design on phones. Do not put that design on category or product cards.

The design image is the print box, in pixels, with object-fit cover (contain for greeting cards). Do not size it from cover-zoom math as an absolutely positioned image larger than the box. A wide screenshot becomes several times the print box, and phones clip that layer away, so a black shirt looks blank.

Do not add `transform: translateZ(0)` on `.product-preview-overlay-clip`. That combination with `overflow: hidden` drops the design on iOS.

Garment color is a tint of the white blank, capped around 400px, delivered as a blob URL. Do not use a full-size PNG data URL. Light colors explode in size, the phone drops the shirt, and the print-box fill shows as a solid square while the tab freezes. If the tint fails, leave the white blank visible. Do not set `crossOrigin` on a blob or data URL.
